💡 **SUGGESTION: third hand-rolled copy of the custom-name match — extract a shared helper**

The registry-leg name match (trim + case-fold the ref, case-fold `entry.name`, first hit wins) now exists in two places: `ModelRolesResolver._findCustomProvider` (`model_resolver.dart`) and the `_refNeedsEndpointSlot` mirror here. Both were introduced by this PR, and they must stay in lockstep forever — if one ever canonicalizes aliases or trims entry names and the other doesn't, the preload set and the resolver silently disagree and the exact "resolves but skips as keyless" failure this PR fixes comes back.

Suggest a single shared helper, e.g. on the entry list:

```dart
extension CustomProviderLookup on List<CustomProviderEntry> {
  CustomProviderEntry? findByChainName(String name) { ... }
}
```

placed next to `CustomProviderEntry` in `custom_providers.dart` so both `startup.dart` and `model_resolver.dart` consume it. (Minor: also consider trimming `entry.name` on both sides — today only the ref side is trimmed.)

